{
  "info": {
    "name": "Koa Auth API",
    "description": "Authentication API with JWT using Koa.js, TypeORM, and PostgreSQL\n\n## Tech Stack\n- **Framework**: Koa.js (Node.js)\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL 16\n- **ORM**: TypeORM\n- **Authentication**: JWT (JSON Web Tokens)\n- **Validation**: Zod\n- **Containerization**: Docker & Docker Compose\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Using Docker (Recommended)\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run docker:dev\n```\nServer will be available at: http://localhost:3000\n\n### Local Development\n1. Install PostgreSQL 16\n2. Configure `.env` file\n3. Run `npm install && npm run dev`\n\n## Authentication Flow\n1. **Register** - Create new account (returns JWT token)\n2. **Login** - Authenticate existing account (returns JWT token)\n3. Use the token in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header for protected routes\n\n## Collection Variables\n- `baseUrl`: API base URL (default: http://localhost:3000/api)\n- `token`: JWT token (auto-saved after Register/Login)\n\n## Notes\n- All `/api/users` routes require JWT authentication\n- Tokens are automatically saved to collection variable after successful login/register\n- Password requirements: min 8 chars, must include uppercase, lowercase, and number",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "koa-auth-api-collection",
    "version": "2.0.0"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000/api",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
